From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cix: scope ACPI platform quirks at runtime

CONFIG_ARCH_CIX selects support in a multiplatform kernel; it does not
identify the running SoC. Keep the generic CPPC, SCMI power-domain,
thermal, SMMUv3 and SBSA watchdog behavior when the Sky1 ACPI SCMI
controller (CIXHA006) is absent. Select the longer SCMI mailbox timeout
from the probed transport device itself.

Keep CIX IPA enabled, but select its power callbacks and firmware methods
only on Sky1 ACPI. Handle a missing SPRG/DPRG method before using its
result, and propagate SMMU suspend/resume errors.

Signed-off-by: Clay Stan <claystan97@gmail.com>
---
